  "answers": {
    "Q1": "handleReadDevDataToFileCmd delegates to readDevCalDataToDisk, which stores the caller-supplied 6568-byte tagDevData and extracts 3 CCF files + activeBox.dat; handleEndCalibComputeCmd only reacts to errorCode==0 by notifying isCalibrated.",
    "Q2": "CCF = 33 LE f64 + optional 64 i32 trailer (520/520/264 B); in-memory record 0xB8 with 22 f64 in order f,c,kc,alpha,R,T; trailer is a per-camera constant, its role unresolved.",
    "Q3": "Both: the 3 files in ./res/Einscan-E10/200x150 are overwritten and the 0xF21 block is written to device offset 0x39B. cameraCalibFlag.dat is a LE QDateTime marker. No factory CCF backup exists. Failures leave files and device inconsistent (no joint rollback).",
    "Q4": "Regenerates all 3 camera CCF records (full overwrite, no merge), but measured data shows kc[5] preserved bit-exactly from factory while f,c,alpha,pose are re-estimated; applied at scan time via load_ccf_binary on <base>/200x150/*.txt (+activeBox/lookupTable), with a devData alternative.",
    "Q5": "Binary LE, 33 f64 in fixed order + 64 i32 trailer, no formatting; writer round-trip reproduces Left/Right byte-identically and loses only the Tex error field; integer-offset keying measured as alpha+2,k2+6,p1+2,p2+7,k3+13 (IR) / 0 (colour).",
    "Q6": "Immutable factory/ snapshot of the raw 6568 B + 3 files; per-revision full copies + assembled 0xF21 block; write order = persist, writeCustomInfo@0x39B, setCalibCCFData, setProjectCalirateTime, cameraCalibFlag last; read back 0x39B..0x12BC and compare."
  },
